    "updated_at": "2025-12-17T09:07:51Z",
    "body": "WebKit in theory supports this distinction, but instead of performing null checks on the resulting string in `HTMLConstructionSite::setCompatibilityModeFromDoctype` it performs empty checks, which encompasses null and the empty string. So even if we go the WebKit (and Chromium) way, there is still some cleanup to be done in those parsers.\n\ncc @josepharhar ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
