    "created_at": "2026-01-08T11:30:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-08T11:30:11Z",
    "body": "When this part of the spec was written, it was very much intended that the distinction was missing / not missing. However, if treating the empty string as missing has not been a problem for Chrome and Safari, I guess that shows that Web compat doesn't care about the empty string case, so we could change the treatment of the empty string to go together with missing instead of going together with not missing and not empty.\n\nThe important thing is that we don't change the behavior for missing and not missing and not empty.\n\nIt's kinda sad WebKit managed to create a quirk in quirk detection (through a string class that doesn't distinguish between empty and not present perhaps)?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
